        {label:"Described figure &mdash; Fig. C3.2.10", text:"A graph of antibody concentration against time shows the primary response rising only after about a 5-day lag (driven by short-lived plasma cells) before falling away; the secondary response, driven by memory cells retained in the lymph nodes, begins with almost no lag and reaches a substantially higher peak."}
